  "question": {
    "text": "A person invites a party of 10 friends at dinner and place so that 4 are on one round table and 6 on the other round table. Total number of ways in which he can arrange the guests is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "1DSNZ",
      "text": "$\\frac{10!}{6!}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nix3j",
      "text": "$\\frac{10!}{24}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "RKbF4",
      "text": "$\\frac{9!}{24}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iD2sY",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Total person $=10$\nTwo groups are formed containing 4 and 6 persons.\n$\\therefore$ Total ways of formation of groups $=\\frac{10!}{4!6!}$\nNow, 4 persons can be arranged on round table\n$=(4-1)!=3!$\nand 6 persons can be arranged on round table $=(6-1)$ !\n$=5!$\n$\\therefore$ Total ways of arranging the guest\n$=\\frac{10!}{4!6!} \\times 3!\\times 5!=\\frac{10!}{24}$",
    "image": null
  },
